    ("tracing-prevents-all-memory-leaks", "Tracing GC removes every application memory leak", "An obsolete value kept reachable by a rooted strong cache remains live to an ordinary tracer. Reachability alone does not tell the collector whether the application will ever use that value again.", "retained-cache"),
    ("copying-needs-no-reference-updates", "A copying collector can move live objects without handling their references", "Every relevant direct reference must be fixed or routed through an adequate handle before old storage reuse. Unregistered aliases, pins and opaque pointers need an explicit relocation policy.", "reference-fixup"),
    ("young-collection-needs-only-direct-roots", "A young-only collection can ignore all old-to-young references", "Strong incoming references from outside the selected subset must be accounted for. Complete remembered information can supply them, while scanning the relevant older population is another valid strategy.", "old-young-edge"),
    ("one-heap-barrier-solves-concurrent-gc", "A heap insertion barrier alone makes any concurrent marker sound", "The barrier must fit the collector's root, allocation, scan, synchronization and termination protocol. The declared fixed-root model does not prove correctness for an arbitrary production collector or a deletion-only barrier.", "insertion-barrier"),
