    ("python314-always-two-generations", "Every CPython 3.14 patch has only two GC generations", "The fixed GIL-enabled CPython 3.14.7 profile has generations 0, 1 and 2, with generation 1 restored in 3.14.5. Initial-3.14 descriptions must not be substituted for that patch's collection policy.", "cycle-collector"),
    ("reference-counting-collects-isolated-cycles", "Reference counting alone reclaims every isolated ownership cycle", "Internal strong owners can keep all counts positive after external owners disappear. Rust Rc has no cyclic collector, while CPython adds collection of eligible tracked cycles to ordinary reference counting.", "strong-cycle"),
    ("weak-keeps-rc-value-alive", "A Weak keeps the Rc value alive after the last strong owner is dropped", "A Weak derived from an existing allocation can retain its backing block, not the stored value's strong lifetime. Upgrade returns None after the strong-owned value is gone; Weak::new has no backing allocation.", "weak-handle"),
